# Citation metadata, in the format GitHub and Zenodo both read.
#
# The same claim appears in two places: this file and the footer of the tool
# itself. Two copies of one string is two chances to disagree, and both are
# meant to be held against src/lib/site.ts, the source for both, by whatever
# check a future change to this repository adds back.
#
# The DOI is minted by Zenodo when the tagged release is archived. Two are
# recorded, on the reference tool's own convention: the concept DOI, which
# always resolves to the newest version and is the one to cite, and the
# version DOI for this specific release. The concept DOI is held against
# CITATION_DOI in src/lib/site.ts.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
title: Molarity Converter for Biologics
abstract: >-
  A deterministic browser tool that converts between mass and molar
  concentration for a protein whose molecular weight the user declares,
  along with its source and what that weight is the mass of. No molecular
  weight is supplied, inferred, defaulted or looked up, and no data entered
  by a user leaves the browser.
authors:
  - family-names: Modi
    given-names: A.B.
    affiliation: Ligant AI Incorporated
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0009-3837-6605
# Matches APP_VERSION in src/lib/site.ts and the tag on the archived release.
# The leading v is kept so that this file, the footer and the tag are the
# same string rather than three conventions for one version.
version: v0.1.1
# The day the tag was cut and the release archived, not the day this file
# was first drafted.
date-released: '2026-09-16'
license: Apache-2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22750471
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22750471
    description: Concept DOI. Resolves to the newest archived version, and is the one to cite.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22750472
    description: Version DOI for v0.1.0.
repository-code: https://github.com/abmodi-ai/Ligant.ai-Molarity-Converter
url: https://benchtools.ligant.ai/molarity-converter/
keywords:
  - molarity
  - mass concentration
  - molar concentration
  - biologics
  - protein
  - antibody
  - reproducible research
